Like believing in people
and people hurting me

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:02.283
and all that stuff, it's made me meaner.

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:06.663
So I'm either gonna hurt somebody,

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:09.290
like for real, for real

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:12.843
and go to prison for the rest of my life.

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:16.880
Because I have all this
built of aggression

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:17.913
on the inside of me.

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:23.283
So if I were to ever just go off,

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:28.883
oh my god, it would
probably be bad, you know?

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.890
Especially the way that I was drinking,

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:37.050
'cause you know, at that point
you get inebriated, right?

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:39.940
And then you're emotion are...

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:45.310
They're heightened, you know?

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:48.660
And you can start off just
a little bit pissed off,

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:49.730
but if you drunk enough,

00:15:49.730 --> 00:15:51.780
oh you turn into the motherfuckin' Hulk.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:52.770
You know what I mean?

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:56.403
I don't wanna hurt anybody,
and I'm tired of being hurt.

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:02.520
So I really feel in my heart
that I'm being released

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:04.353
from Skid Row.

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:06.843
I do.

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:10.843
Because I know that there
was I reason why I was here.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:15.830
And not to toot my own
horn or anything like that,

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:17.763
but I have touched a lot of people.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:23.200
Whether it was good or bad or indifferent.

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:25.363
These motherfuckers are gonna remember me.

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:28.385
Do you know what I mean?

00:16:28.385 --> 00:16:31.893
They will.

00:16:31.893 --> 00:16:33.343
They'll remember me.

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:38.970
And I will remember
every single one of them,

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.883
and I hope that one day,
after I get outta here,

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:47.520
matter of fact I know that
I'm gonna come back here.

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:48.793
I'm gonna give back.

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:54.920
'Cause ironically enough,
before I even came out here,

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:57.823
I used to feed the
homeless on Thanksgiving.

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:03.120
And now I'm the one being
fed on Thanksgiving.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.620
- [Mark] How's that feel?

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:05.453
- Fucked up.

00:17:05.453 --> 00:17:07.921
(Mark chuckles)

00:17:07.921 --> 00:17:09.700
'Cause I remember my first
Thanksgiving out here,

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:14.303
I just cried and cried
and cried and cried.

00:17:16.525 --> 00:17:21.180
And these last two
Thanksgivings and Christmases

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:25.713
have been extra cold and
raining and messed up.

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:30.763
And everybody out here is a scavenger.

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:34.010
And these organizations don't really

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:37.510
have enough for everybody, you know?

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:39.170
- [Mark] I think a lot of my viewers

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:43.520
don't understand the number
of people that are out here.

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:44.353
- Oh god.

00:17:44.353 --> 00:17:46.160
- [Mark] They see 200 videos on my channel

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:47.730
and think, "Oh my god, there's
200 people down there."

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:49.190
- Fuck no.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:51.650
- [Mark] There's like 200,000,

00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:54.750
and I'm just picking the ones
that are the most interesting.

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:55.583
- It's-

00:17:55.583 --> 00:17:56.416
- [Mark] You know what they say,

00:17:56.416 --> 00:17:57.249
"Once you help this person,

00:17:57.249 --> 00:17:59.225
"what about the other 10,000
that are just like her?"

00:17:59.225 --> 00:18:00.058
- Right.

00:18:01.361 --> 00:18:02.610
- [Mark] Of that one person,

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:04.484
you think we're gonna help?

00:18:04.484 --> 00:18:05.595
- Right.

00:18:05.595 --> 00:18:09.713
- [Mark] You're ignoring the other 999-

00:18:09.713 --> 00:18:10.600
(chuckles)

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:11.847
There's so many others
- Right.

00:18:11.847 --> 00:18:12.950
- [Mark] That are just like her.

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:13.783
- Well, what they need to do is

00:18:13.783 --> 00:18:16.010
they need to come and see for themselves.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:16.930
- [Mark] And then again,

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.600
this goes on in every
state of the country.

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.330
Not to the same extent that it is here,

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.910
in maybe San Francisco and LA-
- Absolutely not.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:23.910
- [Mark] Seattle, Portland,

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:26.070
all have really terrible
homeless communities,

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:28.800
but so does New York, New Jersey, Chicago.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:31.450
- They have the river
in Orange County too.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:32.760
The river bed people.

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:34.540
- [Mark] Yeah, so it's
all over the country,

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:35.690
and it's getting worse.

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:39.680
- But it's bad though, there's a lot.

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:42.760
And it's to an extreme,

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:47.690
because I believe that
this is where a lot of

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:53.960
all the crap originated from, you know?

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:55.463
You here all kinds of stories.

00:18:56.985 --> 00:18:59.550
I heard a story from my OG the other day.

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:02.060
He had said, you know the reason-

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:04.160
'cause the rats are aggressive out here.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:06.053
They're not just regular rats.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.223
I call the rats gang bangers.

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:13.740
They're not regular rats.

00:19:13.740 --> 00:19:16.770
And an older guy told me-

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:17.603
- [Mark] They're very bold.

00:19:17.603 --> 00:19:20.270
- You know the reason why
they're bold like that

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:22.770
is because in the 80's we
were feeding them crack.

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:28.220
I said, "What, shut the hell up."

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:30.620
He said, "No, for real."

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:32.220
And if you look it up, even on YouTube,

00:19:32.220 --> 00:19:33.510
and I looked it up on YouTube,

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:36.690
because I wanted to see
what he was talking about.

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:41.690
They've done experiments
on rats with crack cocaine.

00:19:42.690 --> 00:19:47.103
And they will keep going
back for their crack.

00:19:48.010 --> 00:19:50.190
Over and over and over again.

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:52.320
They get addicted very quickly.

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:55.143
And they're bigger than normal.

00:19:56.383 --> 00:19:57.216
Mannn.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.110
I was standing in front
of the store, right?

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:02.993
And I had just-

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:05.690
My friend had just bought me a hamburger,

00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:07.093
and I was really hungry too.

00:20:08.170 --> 00:20:10.210
And I took a bite of it, right?

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:12.170
And I put it on the
wall, I had wrapped it up

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:14.870
and put it on the wall,
because I had to tie my shoe

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:16.543
to fix my backpack, right.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:21.650
This big rat came out

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:26.220
and just took my hamburger

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:31.220
off the wall, like even
the rats are scavengers.

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:35.030
Like even the rats are gang bangers.

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:37.040
They will bite holes in your tent.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:37.873
- [Mark] Oh yeah.

00:20:37.873 --> 00:20:40.453
- They will go in your
tent and eat your food.

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:45.590
Just when you think that everything's okay

00:20:46.820 --> 00:20:49.150
and because you got all
these rat traps around.

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:53.020
No, they're hybrid rats or something,

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:55.510
like something's wrong.

00:20:55.510 --> 00:20:57.370
It's crazy out here, it's crazy.

00:20:57.370 --> 00:20:58.530
'Cause I'm ready to go.

00:20:58.530 --> 00:20:59.923
I was not-

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:04.750
This is not the kind of life that I want.

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:07.430
- [Mark] I'm so happy to
hear you speak like this,

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:10.680
'cause last time we spoke,
you weren't really as

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:13.782
driven to change your situation.

00:21:13.782 --> 00:21:17.174
- No, I really thought that
I was gonna die out here.

00:21:17.174 --> 00:21:19.600
- [Mark] And that positivity, that...

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:24.770
readiness for success is, to me,

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:26.623
the most important part of recovery.

00:21:27.690 --> 00:21:29.000
You need to want...

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:35.610
and just not just want,
but be driven to succeed.

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:39.083
And to be fulfilled and
to have a good life.

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:42.740
I hear that in your voice now.

00:21:43.770 --> 00:21:45.110
You'll be the first...

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:51.343
addict that I'm involved in
doing a donation campaign for.

00:21:52.690 --> 00:21:54.330
Because everything you're saying

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:55.910
tells me that you can do it.

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:56.743
- Yeah well-

00:21:56.743 --> 00:21:57.576
- [Mark] Whereas everyone else I've spoken

00:21:57.576 --> 00:21:58.850
to that's an addict,

00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:00.976
they're ready to stay
right where they're at.

00:22:00.976 --> 00:22:01.890
- They enjoy it.

00:22:01.890 --> 00:22:03.320
- [Mark] They enjoy it,

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:05.790
they might say they want recovery.

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:09.120
- I don't even like to go
in other peoples tents.

00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:12.290
The only time I go in anybody else's tent

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:16.244
is if it's clean or I'm
absolutely desperate.

00:22:16.244 --> 00:22:17.550
- [Mark] No, you're coming around.

00:22:17.550 --> 00:22:19.375
You're coming back to the world.

00:22:19.375 --> 00:22:20.980
- Do you know what I mean?

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:23.670
And then I try to encourage others,

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:26.710
and they all have excuse
after excuse after excuse,

00:22:26.710 --> 00:22:30.593
like I feel free, this is
freedom, I feel good out here.

00:22:31.962 --> 00:22:35.450
And this man tell me the other day that

00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:39.433
he left his dad's birthday party, right?

00:22:40.590 --> 00:22:42.533
To go get a pack of cigarettes.

00:22:43.520 --> 00:22:48.310
Ended up downtown and hasn't
been home in ten years.

00:22:48.310 --> 00:22:49.143
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:22:53.420 --> 00:22:58.420
- You have a home that
you can go to right now,

00:23:00.580 --> 00:23:02.500
and you're choosing methamphetamines,

00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:06.810
and this nasty ass tent
with this dirty ass dog

00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:10.510
over being home?

00:23:10.510 --> 00:23:11.930
- [Mark] Because it
feels like home to them.

00:23:11.930 --> 00:23:13.750
It feels like where they belong.

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:14.583
- Fuck-

00:23:14.583 --> 00:23:15.416
- [Mark] And what's great about

00:23:15.416 --> 00:23:17.100
listening to you talk today is

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:18.003
it's very clear that you feel

00:23:18.003 --> 00:23:19.700
like you don't belong here any longer.

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:20.533
- I don't.

00:23:22.031 --> 00:23:25.300
Fuck that shit, I wanna go back to work,

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:27.130
and I wanna start doing my nails again.

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:30.890
And feeling good about myself again,

00:23:30.890 --> 00:23:34.650
because that's where I lost it at, Mark.

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:37.633
Because I lost my self worth.

00:23:39.002 --> 00:23:40.360
- [Mark] That's how this happens.

00:23:40.360 --> 00:23:41.770
- Right.

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:45.180
Because woman get discouraged, right?

00:23:45.180 --> 00:23:49.031
And then these men keep
them all drugged up,

00:23:49.031 --> 00:23:51.440
and all they wanna do is screw on 'em

00:23:51.440 --> 00:23:55.760
and keep 'em locked up
in a tent, you know?

00:23:55.760 --> 00:23:58.603
I've even seen woman
in cages before, Mark.

00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:01.883
It's bad out here.

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:08.160
Nope, oh no, not me, I can't.

00:24:11.110 --> 00:24:14.193
I can't, I can't.

00:24:15.690 --> 00:24:17.900
Well, anyway one of the things that

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:23.470
a lot of the viewers wanted
to do was hear me sing.

00:24:23.470 --> 00:24:26.319
- [Mark] I'd love to
hear you sing. (chuckles)

00:24:26.319 --> 00:24:28.900
- Now that I'm on blast, I
don't even know what to sing.

00:24:28.900 --> 00:24:29.733
Let me think.

00:24:42.707 --> 00:24:44.290
Oh, here I got one.

00:24:46.680 --> 00:24:49.333
This is from the movie
Fighting Temptations.

00:24:51.470 --> 00:24:52.590
It's actually a Christian movie

00:24:52.590 --> 00:24:54.943
and they have a choir or whatever.

00:24:57.680 --> 00:24:59.840
Beyonce has a part that's awesome.

00:25:00.870 --> 00:25:02.660
And I've actually sung this

00:25:02.660 --> 00:25:04.540
while walking down the street before

00:25:06.010 --> 00:25:08.743
in the middle of the night, cold as hell.

00:25:10.120 --> 00:25:12.673
Because one thing-

00:25:14.790 --> 00:25:16.090
music makes me happy.

00:25:16.090 --> 00:25:18.807
Remember how I said in my last video,

00:25:18.807 --> 00:25:20.730
"As long as I got my music and my alcohol

00:25:20.730 --> 00:25:22.380
and my cigarettes, I'm straight."

00:25:25.080 --> 00:25:26.483
As long as I have music,

00:25:27.460 --> 00:25:31.123
because what it does is it
never lets me down, right?

00:25:32.923 --> 00:25:36.177
It never lets me down and
it helps me feel, you know?

00:25:38.250 --> 00:25:41.953
I'm no longer numb because
it's something that I love.

00:25:45.940 --> 00:25:47.240
It's something I love.

00:25:47.240 --> 00:25:51.590
So I will sing in the middle of the day,

00:25:51.590 --> 00:25:54.790
in the middle of the night
at the top of my lungs.

00:25:54.790 --> 00:25:56.683
I don't give a damn, I'm gonna sing.

00:25:58.570 --> 00:26:00.310
But she says-

00:26:00.310 --> 00:26:02.610
Especially because of
what she says, she says-

00:26:05.806 --> 00:26:07.470
'Cuse me, I smoke a lot in Newports,

00:26:07.470 --> 00:26:09.120
that's one thing I have not quit.

00:26:10.073 --> 00:26:11.250
(chuckles)

00:26:11.250 --> 00:26:12.083
She said,

00:26:14.496 --> 00:26:18.884
♪ I used to wake up some days ♪

00:26:18.884 --> 00:26:21.851
♪ And wish I'd stayed asleep ♪

00:26:21.851 --> 00:26:25.072
♪ 'Cause I went to bed
on top of the world ♪

00:26:25.072 --> 00:26:28.318
♪ Today the worlds on top of me ♪

00:26:28.318 --> 00:26:31.369
♪ Everybody's got opinions ♪

00:26:31.369 --> 00:26:34.484
♪ Y'all ain't been in my position ♪

00:26:34.484 --> 00:26:36.114
♪ So I laugh at the world ♪

00:26:36.114 --> 00:26:40.547
♪ When I hear what they
have to say about me ♪

00:26:40.547 --> 00:26:45.547
♪ Feels like I always fall
short of bein' worthy ♪

00:26:47.448 --> 00:26:50.186
♪ 'Cause I ain't good enough ♪

00:26:50.186 --> 00:26:52.368
♪ But you still love me ♪

00:26:52.368 --> 00:26:54.422
♪ I ain't no superstar ♪

00:26:54.422 --> 00:26:58.172
♪ The spotlight ain't shinin' on me ♪

00:26:58.172 --> 00:27:00.873
♪ 'Cause I ain't good enough ♪

00:27:00.873 --> 00:27:02.665
♪ But you still love me ♪

00:27:02.665 --> 00:27:05.640
♪ I'm not perfect ♪

00:27:05.640 --> 00:27:08.432
♪ Yes I do wrong ♪

00:27:08.432 --> 00:27:10.697
♪ I've been trying my best ♪

00:27:10.697 --> 00:27:14.578
♪ But it ain't good enough ♪

00:27:14.578 --> 00:27:17.423
♪ Shunned by the world ♪

00:27:17.423 --> 00:27:20.653
♪ If I don't succeed ♪

00:27:20.653 --> 00:27:23.893
♪ Though I ain't good enough ♪

00:27:23.893 --> 00:27:27.530
♪ He still loves me ♪

00:27:27.530 --> 00:27:32.530
- Man, that's like one
of my favorite songs.

00:27:37.844 --> 00:27:38.677
- [Interviewer] All right, Niqi.

00:27:38.677 --> 00:27:40.090
We're gonna do something
to help you out of there.

00:27:40.090 --> 00:27:40.923
- All right.

00:27:42.209 --> 00:27:44.445
What we gonna do?

00:27:44.445 --> 00:27:46.095
You gotta help me up, I got hurt.

00:27:48.128 --> 00:27:49.150
- [Mark] Good job.

00:27:49.150 --> 00:27:49.983
- [Niqi] Thank you.

00:27:49.983 --> 00:27:52.106
- [Mark] I'm proud of you.

